DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250515
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250516
SUMMARY:Federal: 990-N due
DESCRIPTION:15th day of the 5th month after the close of the accounting per
 iod | Form 990-N for a calendar-year small exempt organization is due May 1
 5\, 2026\, same as the 990/990-EZ/990-PF due date. Unlike those forms\, the
  990-N due date cannot be extended - there is no extension mechanism\, thou
 gh the IRS states there is no penalty for late submission unless it is the 
 organization's third consecutive missed year (which triggers automatic revo
 cation of exempt status). | Authority: IRS: "The 990-N due date cannot be e
 xtended\, but there is no penalty for submitting it late unless it's the th
 ird (and only) year." | Source: https://www.irs.gov/charities-non-profits/a
 nnual-exempt-organization-return-due-date | This date is computed from a re
 currence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm agains
 t the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
